  "faqTitle": "Questions people ask",
  "faqQ1": "Does this cost me anything?",
  "faqA1": "No. Putting your products up is free. The marketplace takes a small share only when something sells.",
  "faqQ2": "What if I have no network?",
  "faqA2": "Everything keeps working. What you make is kept on your phone and sent by itself when the network comes back.",
  "faqQ3": "Who gets my money?",
  "faqA3": "You do. The buyer pays on the marketplace and it comes to your account. The money never passes through us.",
  "faqQ4": "Can I change something after it is on sale?",
  "faqA4": "Yes. Open it from your products, change what you want, and it goes back on sale.",
  "faqQ5": "What if I said something wrong?",
  "faqA5": "Nothing goes on sale until you have heard it back and said it is right. You can correct any part of it by speaking.",
  "faqQ6": "Do I have to read or write?",
  "faqA6": "No. You can do everything by speaking and pressing. Every screen can be read out to you.",
  "faqQ7": "Who sees my name and my village?",
  "faqA7": "Only if you allow it, for each product. You can take that back at any time.",
  "aboutTitle": "About Kirtikar",
  "aboutWhatTitle": "What this is",
  "aboutWhat": "Kirtikar puts handmade work on ONDC, India's open network for buying and selling, by letting the maker speak instead of type. Photos and a voice note in your own language become a listing that buyers across the country can find.",
  "aboutWhyTitle": "Why we built it",
  "aboutWhy": "Around seven million artisans in India make things people want to buy, and most of them sell through a middleman who takes the difference. The barrier is not the work. It is the form: an online listing asks for typed English, a bank of fields, and a photograph shot like a catalogue. This app removes that form.",
  "aboutHowTitle": "How it works",
  "aboutHow": "Take three photos and say what it is. Our pipeline listens, writes the listing, and reads it back to you. Nothing goes out until you have heard it and said it is right.",
  "aboutSihTitle": "Smart India Hackathon 2025",
  "aboutSih": "Built for problem statement 090: helping artisans and weavers reach buyers on ONDC.",
  "aboutMissionTitle": "What we are trying to do",
  "aboutMission": "Put the price of a piece of work in the hands of the person who made it.",
  "supportTitle": "Talk to a person",
  "supportBody": "If something is not working, or you are not sure what to do, call us. A person answers, in your language.",
